      "marks": 1,
      "language": "en",
      "content": {
        "stem": "At t = 0 a particle is at x = 0. It moves along a line with constant acceleration and reaches x = 10 m at t = 2 s and x = 30 m at t = 4 s. What is its acceleration?",
        "options": {
          "A": "7.5 m/s²",
          "B": "1.25 m/s²",
          "C": "5 m/s²",
          "D": "2.5 m/s²"
        },
        "answerKey": "D",
        "solution": "Using x = ut + at²/2 gives 2u + 2a = 10 and 4u + 8a = 30. Doubling the first equation and subtracting it from the second gives 4a = 10, hence a = 2.5 m/s²."
      },
