      "type": "MCQ_SINGLE",
      "difficulty": "HARD",
      "marks": 1,
      "language": "en",
      "content": {
        "stem": "A particle's position on a straight line is x(t) = t³ - 6t² + 9t metres for 0 ≤ t ≤ 4 s. What total distance does it travel in that interval?",
        "options": {
          "A": "4 m",
          "B": "12 m",
          "C": "8 m",
          "D": "16 m"
        },
        "answerKey": "B",
        "solution": "v = dx/dt = 3(t - 1)(t - 3), so direction changes at 1 s and 3 s. Positions are x(0)=0, x(1)=4, x(3)=0, x(4)=4 m. Total distance is |4-0| + |0-4| + |4-0| = 12 m."
      },
