        "conceptIds": []
      },
      "type": "MCQ_SINGLE",
      "difficulty": "HARD",
      "marks": 1,
      "language": "en",
      "content": {
        "stem": "Along one straight track, east is positive. At t = 0, cart A is at x = 0 and starts from rest with constant acceleration +2 m/s². Cart B is at x = 8 m and keeps velocity -2 m/s. What is their relative speed immediately before they meet?",
        "options": {
          "A": "4 m/s",
          "B": "2 m/s",
          "C": "6 m/s",
          "D": "8 m/s"
        },
        "answerKey": "C",
        "solution": "Their positions are x_A = t² and x_B = 8 - 2t. Setting them equal gives t² + 2t - 8 = 0, whose nonnegative root is t = 2 s. Then v_A = 2t = +4 m/s and v_B = -2 m/s; their relative speed is |4 - (-2)| = 6 m/s."
      },
      "tags": [
        "kinematics",
        "straight-line-motion",
        "relative-motion-in-a-straight-line"
      ],
